### 1. Create a card payment
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/payment-orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "debtorAccount": "DE89370400440532013000",
  "creditorAccount": "DE75512108001245126199",
  "amount": 100.00,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "method": "CARD",
  "reference": "Invoice 2026-001"
}

> {% client.global.set("orderId", response.body.id); %}

### 2. Execute it (SETTLED, fee 1.65)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/payment-orders/{{orderId}}/execute

### 3. Read it
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/payment-orders/{{orderId}}

### 4. Refund it (works for CARD and WALLET)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/payment-orders/{{orderId}}/refund

### 5. Execute again: 409, the order is no longer CREATED
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/payment-orders/{{orderId}}/execute

### 6. SEPA in USD: 422, rejected by AllowedCurrencyRule
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/payment-orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "debtorAccount": "DE89370400440532013000",
  "creditorAccount": "DE75512108001245126199",
  "amount": 10.00,
  "currency": "USD",
  "method": "SEPA_CREDIT_TRANSFER"
}

### 7. Wallet above the simulated balance: created, then FAILED on execute
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/payment-orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "debtorAccount": "DE89370400440532013000",
  "creditorAccount": "DE75512108001245126199",
  "amount": 1500.00,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "method": "WALLET"
}

> {% client.global.set("walletOrderId", response.body.id); %}

### 8.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/payment-orders/{{walletOrderId}}/execute
